hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1585","I am Abu Bishr Al-Wasiti, from Khaled, meaning Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: A Jew entered the Prophet’s house. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: May peace be upon you. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “And upon you.” Aisha said: I decided to speak, but I knew the hatred of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for that, so I remained silent, then another one came in and said: Al-Saam. On you, so he said: “And on you,” so I decided to speak, and I knew that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, hated that. Then the third came in and said: May peace be upon you. I was not patient until I said: May peace be upon you and the wrath and curse of God be upon you, brothers of apes and pigs. Do you live? Why did God not revive the Messenger of God? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God does not like indecency and obscenity.” They said something, and we responded to them. “Indeed, the Jews are an envious people.” And they do not envy us for anything as they envy us for peace, and Amen.”"
